=== PHASE P17 PARITY AUDIT (png.c) ===
Source: Source/render/decoders/png.lua (PNGDecoder) — ported faithfully.

Scope:
- Signature check: len<24 reject; data[0]==0x89 + "PNG" magic.            [G.short_input / G.bad_signature]
- Chunk walk: pos=9 1-based → pos=8 0-based; chunkLen BE32; missing len→0;
  `pos > #data+12` break quirk preserved ((long long)pos > len+12).
- IHDR offsets 0/4/8/9/12 (bitDepth/colorType/interlace defaults 8/0/0).  [D.* dims]
- PLTE numColors=len/3, palette gray via rgbToGray, paletteA=255.
- tRNS raw copy; ct3 per-entry alpha applied; ct0 key byte (#>=2);
  ct2 RGB triple bytes 1/3/5 (#>=6) vs RAW high bytes.                    [D.pal / D.rgba]
- IDAT concat into growable buffer; IEND break.
- maxW/maxH <=0 → 360/200; channels map {2:3,3:1,4:2,6:4} else 1.
- Interlace==1: first Adam7 pass only, srcW/H=ceil(dim/8) min 1.          [D.adam7 33x17 -> 5x3]
- rowBytes=(srcW*channels*bd+7)/8; bppBytes=max(1,ch*bd/8); sampleBytes=max(1,bd/8).
- Streaming decode via inflate_stream (createStream parity), scale_accum
  box filter; prevRow zeroed / curRow swap each row.
- Filters: none/sub/up/avg/paeth with a/b/c edge rules; type>4 = copy.    [all fixtures cycle filters 0..4]
- bd<8 packed MSB-first unpack ×grayScale=255//mask integer div.          [D.gray1]
- ct0 bd16 high-byte sampling; ct4 stride 4/2 alpha at p+2/p+1 OOB→255.   [D.gray16 / D.ga]
- ct2/ct6 step 3/4 base=x*step*sb; tRNSkey exact match→255;               [D.rgba]
  composite(g,a): >=255→g, <=0→255, floor((g*a+255*(255-a))/255+0.5).
- finish count==0 → reject; rows handed off as byte grid.
- Device wrapper png_decode → dither_to_image bitmap (P15 reuse).

Fixtures (tools/gen_png_fixtures.py → selftest_png_fixtures.h):
red/rgba/pal/gray8/gray1/ga/gray16/adam7/bench/down + PngProbe goldens.

Port bugs found & fixed during bring-up:
1) USE-AFTER-FREE: idat freed right after inflate_stream_new, but the
   bitstream aliases the buffer (C buffers are not Lua values). Fixed:
   free after decode loop. Diagnosed via /tmp/pngdump on fx_red
   (only the large fixture survived stale-heap luck).

